  "finalText": "The quote is built as a 10-second kinetic type piece on a dark background, with four phrases handing off cleanly and the attribution last.\n\n- **Phrase 1, \"Design is not just\"** (white, 0.2 s): words slide up one by one, then exit upward.\n- **Phrase 2, \"what it looks like.\"** (grey): same word reveal, starting as phrase 1 leaves.\n- **Phrase 3, \"Design is\"** (white): same reveal, starting as phrase 2 leaves.\n- **Hero, \"how it / works.\"** (red, 210 px, about 2x the setup size): letters rise in one by one from 6.7 s, so the punchline is the largest and most saturated element.\n- **Attribution, \"— Steve Jobs\"** (small grey, 28 px): fades in at about 8.5 s.\n\nI extended the composition from 8 s to 10 s so each phrase holds long enough to read. The phrases are on separate layers, named \"Phrase 1 · …\", \"Hero · …\" and \"Attribution · …\", so you can retime them individually.\n\nThe last critique scored it 58/100. The remaining flags are that phrases 1 and 2 hold about 1.2–1.3 s (a bit short of the 1.4 s it wants), phrase 3 holds about 0.75 s, and nothing has overshoot or settle motion. I'd lengthen the holds by roughly 0.2 s each if you want to take that, and I can add a settle on the hero if you want more life in the final frame."
